          "id": "1773674464473",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773674464475_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant who writes professional descriptions for algorithms. Your primary task is to define a long description, less than 1000 characters, for a user about what Oracle's algorithm \"{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.AlgorithmType}}\" is all about based on the algorithm name \"{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.AlgorithmName}}\"\n\nGood example:  \nThe Create Customer and Enter Accounts Receivables Invoice access algorithm systematically identifies all users who possess the capability to execute both the \"Create Customer\" and \"Enter Accounts Receivables Invoice\" functions within the Order to Cash process. This analysis is conducted to detect potential segregation of duties (SoD) conflicts and to ensure compliance with internal controls that mitigate financial risk.\n\nBy cross-referencing user entitlements, the algorithm highlights individuals or roles with access to these potentially conflicting functions, enabling targeted review and remediation by system administrators or audit teams. The goal is to promote process integrity and safeguard against fraudulent or erroneous activities by ensuring that no single user can initiate and complete critical steps within the accounts receivable lifecycle without appropriate oversight.\n\nThe results of this algorithm support proactive access management and continuous monitoring efforts by providing clear, actionable information for access review, user provisioning, and control enforcement. This contributes to the company’s commitment to upholding robust internal controls and facilitating compliance with applicable regulatory standards."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"Description\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
